      "H1": "OCR > OC on E1 AND E2 (prompt effect inside orche; co-primary, intersection-union)",
      "H2": "OCR > PCR on E1 AND E2 (matched-instruction harness comparison), tested only if H1 CONFIRMED (fixed sequence, one-sided 0.025, no alpha split)"
    },
    "inference": "stats.mjs: per family f, x_f = sum over tasks of the paired difference (E1 k_A-k_B, E2 all-3 indicator difference); estimate = sum x_f / (u N) (task-weighted); exact family-level sign-flip test of sum x_f by dynamic programming (no Monte Carlo); per endpoint pass = exact one-sided p < 0.025; 95% interval = inversion of the same exact test under a constant per-task shift (grid 1/300), reported with its acceptance-set check; the decision uses only the exact p values",
    "decision": "stats.mjs coPrimaryDecision / hierarchy (CONFIRMED / NOT_CONFIRMED_HARM_INDICATED / INCONCLUSIVE; H2 NOT_TESTED unless H1 CONFIRMED)",
    "adoption": "unchanged from ctrl-confirm-2 (experiments/ctrl-confirm-2/lib.mjs adoption): ADOPTION_CANDIDATE only if H1 CONFIRMED and no leak/crash/route violation in OCR, OCR legacy and strict failures <= OC, no family regression and no functional point loss (else USER_REVIEW); otherwise KEEP_STABLE; never an automatic deployment",
    "secondaryOutcomes": [
      "strict-valid (byte-identical original tests) E1/E2 per arm and per contrast (sensitivity; disclosure differs between arms, so strict contrasts confound disclosure of the stricter rule)",
